        "q4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is cedar good for outdoor planters?",
            "answer": "<p>It’s one of the best woods you can use outdoors. Cedar is rot-resistant without chemical treatment, holds up to our Pacific Northwest weather, and ages to a soft silver-grey if left untreated or keeps its warm tone if sealed.</p>"
